{"title":"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a competition, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> contestants and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> judges, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedbba3f83fbfdd0b085070b62aae746f0885744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> is an odd\ninteger. Each judge rates each contestant as either “pass” or “fail”. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />\nis a number such that, for any two judges, their ratings coincide for at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />\ncontestants. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/6239ddba3e46e54ef2d766f6e06c038e262ce726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{a}\\ge\\frac{b-1}{2b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e95be43c04d6869c67861aae1e3e69123fedd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> stand for the number of judges who pass the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th candidate. The number of pairs of judges who agree on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th contestant is then given by\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n{c_i \\choose 2} + {{b - c_i} \\choose 2} &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left(c_i(c_i - 1) + (b - c_i)(b - c_i - 1) \\right) \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left( c_i^2 + (b - c_i)^2 - b \\right) \\\\\n&amp;\\geq \\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\frac{b^2}{2} - b \\right) \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{b^2 - 2b}{4}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>where the inequality follows from AM-QM. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee248bf8cc46a67ea26005c67adf2c116917e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and we can strengthen the inequality to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b171b18ac10a2c0f0a7bbd1eabf1410edeba864b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{c_i \\choose 2} + {{b - c_i} \\choose 2} \\geq \\frac{b^2 - 2b + 1}{4} = \\left(\\frac{b - 1}{2}\\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> stand for the number of instances where two judges agreed on a candidate, it follows that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2364f4214f7010c2137216e277e6e54722e63e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\sum_{i = 1}^a {c_i \\choose 2} + {{b - c_i} \\choose 2} \\geq a \\cdot \\left( \\frac{b - 1}{2} \\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"53\" /> \n</p><p>The given condition on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> implies that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d822e4cde94139c63856f9ca61185a3157b3afb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N \\leq k \\cdot {b \\choose 2} = \\frac{kb(b - 1)}{2}.\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Therefore\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/6/c66c6465bc61dc52b9e264ec903870f9bd984f66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\cdot \\left( \\frac{b - 1}{2} \\right)^2 \\leq \\frac{kb(b - 1)}{2},\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>which simplifies to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b3122f2a058fc60b564edde0125e319f117b2450.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k}{a} \\geq \\frac{b - 1}{2b}.\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO\" title=\"1998 IMO\">1998 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191913\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 sec